      "sourceUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50576609",
      "textRawHtml": "These proofs really are quite huge. The proof is 1.3GB, ~15M lines of code:<p></p><pre><code>  mkdir -p riemann_proof &amp;&amp; cd riemann_proof\n\n  # fetch parts 01–14\n  for i in {01..14}; do\n    curl -fSL -o lean.tar.gz.part$i https://alpo.ge/lean.tar.gz.part$i || { echo \"failed: part$i\"; break; }\n  done\n\n  # join and decompress (creates ./lean)\n  cat lean.tar.gz.part{01..14} &gt; lean.tar.gz\n  tar xzf lean.tar.gz\n\n  # size, file count, line counts\n  du -sh lean | cut -f1 | xargs printf '%s on disk (lean folder)\\n'\n  find lean -name '*.lean' | wc -l | xargs printf '%s .lean files\\n'\n  find lean -name '*.lean' -print0 | xargs -0 cat | wc -l | xargs printf '%s lines total\\n'\n  find lean -name '*.lean' -print0 | xargs -0 cat | grep -cv '^[[:space:]]*$' | xargs printf '%s non-blank lines\\n'</code></pre>",
      "textZhHtml": "These proofs really are quite huge. The proof is 1.3GB, ~15M lines of code:<p></p><pre><code>  mkdir -p riemann_proof &amp;&amp; cd riemann_proof\n\n  # fetch parts 01–14\n  for i in {01..14}; do\n    curl -fSL -o lean.tar.gz.part$i https://alpo.ge/lean.tar.gz.part$i || { echo \"failed: part$i\"; break; }\n  done\n\n  # join and decompress (creates ./lean)\n  cat lean.tar.gz.part{01..14} &gt; lean.tar.gz\n  tar xzf lean.tar.gz\n\n  # size, file count, line counts\n  du -sh lean | cut -f1 | xargs printf '%s on disk (lean folder)\\n'\n  find lean -name '*.lean' | wc -l | xargs printf '%s .lean files\\n'\n  find lean -name '*.lean' -print0 | xargs -0 cat | wc -l | xargs printf '%s lines total\\n'\n  find lean -name '*.lean' -print0 | xargs -0 cat | grep -cv '^[[:space:]]*$' | xargs printf '%s non-blank lines\\n'</code></pre>",
      "translationStatus": "translated",
      "contentHash": "48314c8420ad6f81bb345159d233f4646d73f4a2964d706cad99da8ea9ee31b4",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": 50580197,
          "commentKey": "hackernews-50580197",
          "parentId": 50576609,
          "author": "hafeoz",
          "publishedAt": "2026-11-20T19:10:19.000Z",
          "level": 2,
          "hnUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50580197",
          "sourceUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50580197",
          "textRawHtml": "Finally finished compiling on my PC (well, actually an HPC machine at my company, but it's the weekend, and I hope nobody is using it) - it took 2.4 hours on a 480-core Xeon and produced 89 GB of compilation output. I had to make some modifications because, for some reason, Lake bottlenecks and stalls verification. I worked around this by compiling the files directly instead of using `lake build`. I also had to increase `vm.max_map_count` for some later modules.<p>All 175,187 modules seem to check out with Lean 4.33.1, with no errors or `sorry`. There are tons of linter warnings - over 460k of them - but I think they might be caused by the way I invoked it. I haven't checked the actual axiom being proved, though - I'm not good at math :)</p>",
          "textZhHtml": "Finally finished compiling on my PC (well, actually an HPC machine at my company, but it's the weekend, and I hope nobody is using it) - it took 2.4 hours on a 480-core Xeon and produced 89 GB of compilation output. I had to make some modifications because, for some reason, Lake bottlenecks and stalls verification. I worked around this by compiling the files directly instead of using `lake build`. I also had to increase `vm.max_map_count` for some later modules.<p>All 175,187 modules seem to check out with Lean 4.33.1, with no errors or `sorry`. There are tons of linter warnings - over 460k of them - but I think they might be caused by the way I invoked it. I haven't checked the actual axiom being proved, though - I'm not good at math :)</p>",
          "translationStatus": "translated",
          "contentHash": "0f1997934ab5b2bf65b7eee880320ec8e71d2c5087ec90cd97f39c9797f33dc4",
          "children": [
            {
              "id": 50585062,
              "commentKey": "hackernews-50585062",
              "parentId": 50580197,
              "author": "jychang",
              "publishedAt": "2026-11-21T01:54:58.000Z",
              "level": 3,
              "hnUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50585062",
              "sourceUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50585062",
              "textRawHtml": "175,187 modules... a lot of them are repetitive.<p>It really seems he was rushed to publish and did not bother cleaning the code up at all. I am compiling the code and reviewing it, and there are 204 dead modules that are not referenced anywhere. And a LOT of repetitive code.</p><p>I think this should not be 17 million lines, I bet this can easily be under 1 million lines of Lean with a little bit of cleanup.</p>",
              "textZhHtml": "175,187 modules... a lot of them are repetitive.<p>It really seems he was rushed to publish and did not bother cleaning the code up at all. I am compiling the code and reviewing it, and there are 204 dead modules that are not referenced anywhere. And a LOT of repetitive code.</p><p>I think this should not be 17 million lines, I bet this can easily be under 1 million lines of Lean with a little bit of cleanup.</p>",
              "translationStatus": "translated",
              "contentHash": "de7461a8fd30f7fb0bf280ffe41ab5281283e819fdd6ab3198c13cb179a974e8",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": 50587051,
                  "commentKey": "hackernews-50587051",
                  "parentId": 50585062,
                  "author": "fspeech",
                  "publishedAt": "2026-11-21T08:04:14.000Z",
                  "level": 4,
                  "hnUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50587051",
                  "sourceUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50587051",
                  "textRawHtml": "It is probably not that compressible. Anthropic FLT proof also has a lot of redundancies but my projection is without true mathematical refactoring it will be hard to get to 50% reduction in line count. One problem is that Lean, or type theory really, is truly verbose. In these parallely developed proofs if two agents use slightly incompatible definitions there are a lot of translations back and forth. Also FLT is following routes well established by mathematicians and it still got to 13 million lines. So I am actually surprised that GRH is not much bigger, as it reportedly ranges over a wide swath of fields.",
                  "textZhHtml": "It is probably not that compressible. Anthropic FLT proof also has a lot of redundancies but my projection is without true mathematical refactoring it will be hard to get to 50% reduction in line count. One problem is that Lean, or type theory really, is truly verbose. In these parallely developed proofs if two agents use slightly incompatible definitions there are a lot of translations back and forth. Also FLT is following routes well established by mathematicians and it still got to 13 million lines. So I am actually surprised that GRH is not much bigger, as it reportedly ranges over a wide swath of fields.",
                  "translationStatus": "translated",
                  "contentHash": "ac65b2b225f26f5b89797b7c5111030b6df110a9cadda4c695e9ff9894081f38",
                  "children": [
