                          "sourceUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50590969",
                          "textRawHtml": "Yes it would be interesting to see that version. If compaction comes from proof architectural improvement (what I  called \"true mathematical refactoring\"), it could improve readability. On the other hand if it is tactical, for example using tall rw stacks that are incomprehensible to humans, shortness doesn't necessarily imply better accessibility. I suppose it has to be a lot of the first kind to get that much compression.",
                          "textZhHtml": "Yes it would be interesting to see that version. If compaction comes from proof architectural improvement (what I  called \"true mathematical refactoring\"), it could improve readability. On the other hand if it is tactical, for example using tall rw stacks that are incomprehensible to humans, shortness doesn't necessarily imply better accessibility. I suppose it has to be a lot of the first kind to get that much compression.",
