                  "hnUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50585636",
                  "sourceUrl": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50585636",
                  "textRawHtml": "I probably shouldn't say this, but I work at a company related to CPU manufacturing.<p>Part of my job is to ensure that HPC programs (largely LLM libraries these days) work on their next-generation CPUs and with new BIOS revisions. We test them using a shared pool of machines with various configurations. GPU machines are much scarcer, and we have to share them with other teams, so it's hard to reserve a time slot. I usually reserve a CPU machine around the clock so I can work whenever I want (I'm more productive at midnight), and nobody seems to mind.</p><p>I've worked here for almost a year now, and I love my company ;)</p>",
                  "textZhHtml": "I probably shouldn't say this, but I work at a company related to CPU manufacturing.<p>Part of my job is to ensure that HPC programs (largely LLM libraries these days) work on their next-generation CPUs and with new BIOS revisions. We test them using a shared pool of machines with various configurations. GPU machines are much scarcer, and we have to share them with other teams, so it's hard to reserve a time slot. I usually reserve a CPU machine around the clock so I can work whenever I want (I'm more productive at midnight), and nobody seems to mind.</p><p>I've worked here for almost a year now, and I love my company ;)</p>",
